# Build artifacts
build/
# ...except the tool-pin file the Makefile includes: an image that runs make
# (the integration stage's entrypoint) cannot parse the Makefile without it.
!build/docker/devcontainer/tool-pins.env
*.test
*.out

# Coverage reports
coverage.out
coverage.html

# Temporary files
*.tmp
*.img
/tmp/

# Git
.git/
.gitignore

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# Code-analysis tooling scratch state (#66). Untracked and gitignored, but it
# still exists in a developer's working directory, and
# the integration stage of build/docker/devcontainer/Dockerfile ends in
# `COPY . .` — so without this
# line a local `make integration-test` bakes the tool's notes into an image
# layer.
.serena/

# Files tracked on main that the public release does not carry: the
# strip-at-publish list (DefaultStripAtPublish in
# test/internal/labstrings/published.go), which .gitattributes export-ignores.
# A broad COPY must not bake them into a layer either.
# test/tools/releasability-gate/export_test.go requires every entry here, and
# for a directory entry (`<dir>/**`) the directory itself as well, as in
# .gitattributes.
**/CLAUDE.md
**/AGENTS.md
**/.claude/**
**/.claude
**/.serena/**
**/.serena
.github/workflows/code-review.yml
test/internal/labstrings/fleet.go
test/internal/labstrings/fleet_test.go

# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# BuildKit credential staging file. The private-module credential pattern
# mounts those variables via --mount=type=secret and the file is meant to live
# OUTSIDE the build context; this line is the second line of defence, so that a
# copy landing in the tree by accident can never be baked into a layer by a
# broad COPY.
gomodauth*
